NTRTL -- NT Runtime Library

The NT Runtime Library provides core runtime functionality following Windows NT
conventions for use throughout the A•NUX Project (APXH bootloader, NUX kernel,
and user-space applications).

NTRTL includes:
- String manipulation (ANSI and Unicode/UTF-16)
- Memory management functions
- Bitmap operations
- Linked list management
- Red-black tree implementation
- Architecture-optimized assembly implementations (amd64, i386, riscv64)

All NTRTL functions follow NT naming conventions (RtlXxx) and use the ANXAPI
calling convention for consistency across platforms and compilers.

